# Build context for both images (server/Dockerfile and client/Dockerfile are
# built from the repository root, because each depends on `shared/` and the
# root lockfile).
#
# Secrets first: a local .env must never reach an image layer, where anyone
# who pulls the image can read it. The images get their configuration from
# the platform (Render, Kubernetes, docker compose) at run time instead.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Installed and generated files: the Dockerfiles install and build their own,
# for Linux, from the lockfile.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report

# Local recordings (the no-Cloudinary storage path) and caches.
**/.data
**/.cache

# Repository and editor metadata, docs and tooling the images never read.
.git
.github
.husky
.vscode
.idea
.claude
docs
e2e
k8s
helm
loadtest
**/*.md
**/Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
